l,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":null,"_score_margin_vs_hist":null,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":-0.49087138848439826,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":1.0,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":100.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.13540162021414207,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":78.5,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.18771648925251458,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.10241,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":68.3,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Astera Labs, Inc. designs, manufactures, and sells semiconductor-based connectivity solutions for cloud and AI infrastructure in Taiwan and the United States. It offers an intelligent connectivity platform, comprised of semiconductor-based, high-speed, mixed-signal connectivity products that integrate a matrix of microcontrollers and sensors, and COSMOS. The company provides COSMOS software suite, a connectivity system management and optimization software that enables management and optimization of resources for large fleets at cloud-scale via link, fleet, and RAS management capabilities. In addition, it offers PCIe/CXL smart DSP retimers and cable modules; ethernet smart cable modules for cloud and AI infrastructure; CXL memory connectivity controllers; and smart fabric switches. The company serves hyperscalers and system original equipment manufacturers. Astera Labs, Inc. was incorporated in 2017 and is based in San Jose, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jitendra  Mohan | Co-Founder, CEO & Executive Director | Age 51 | Compensation: $2.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 756 people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers. Each employee generates $373K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $212K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Astera Labs, Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $38.8B market cap on $853M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +115% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +49.6pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -38% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 76% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $282M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 33 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.46\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 19% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 10% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 474% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":4.74175880682022},{"text":"Beneish M-Score flags potential earnings manipulation \u2014 a question of whether the reported numbers can be trusted","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.0% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $216.8M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Technology peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 14% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Gross margin tops the Technology peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Growing faster than most Technology peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Among the least levered in Technology \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Astera Labs (ALAB) Record Quarter Puts Its Fair Value Narrative Back In Focus","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/semiconductors/nasdaq-alab/astera-labs/news/astera-labs-alab-record-quarter-puts-its-fair-value-narrativ","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794569554.132,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.886,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"ALAB Benefits From Strong PCIe Demand: Can It Beat MRVL & CRDO?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3028980/alab-benefits-from-strong-pcie-demand-can-it-beat-mrvl-crdo?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Cquick_take-3028980","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794503400.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.66,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Need To Know: Analysts Are Much More Bullish On Astera Labs, Inc. (NASDAQ:ALAB) Revenues","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/semiconductors/nasdaq-alab/astera-labs/news/need-to-know-analysts-are-much-more-bullish-on-astera-labs-i-1","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794479073.923,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Astera Labs (NASDAQ:ALAB) Shares Climb 6.8% \u2013 Should You Buy?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/astera-labs-nasdaqalab-shares-climb-6-8-should-you-buy.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794436873.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.866,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is Astera Labs (NASDAQ:ALAB) Riding AI Connectivity Demand?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/arti